emacs is the extensible editor. This sheet combines the current Emacs/Evil
configuration with stable Emacs defaults. Keys marked Hydra are active after
the prefix shown; Evil keys apply in Evil Normal/Insert states.

Global and minibuffer:
	M-x - Execute an extended command
	C-g - Quit/cancel the current command
	C-x C-f - Find/open a file; C-x C-s - Save the buffer
	C-x C-b or C-x b - Open Ibuffer
	C-x 2 / C-x 3 - Split below/right; C-x 1 - Keep one window
	C-x o - Select the next window (ace-window is configured)
	C-x u - Undo; C-s / C-r - Search forward/backward
	M-/ - Hippie expand
	C-x C-l - Complete a line from the project/buffer
	C-c C-l - Complete a line from the current buffer
	C-c C-; - Complete multiple lines
	C-x C-z - Switch to a shell; C-x C-m - Execute a command
	C-q - Open a line for snippet expansion; C-x C-o - Find a file at point
	C-M-s / C-M-r - Regular-expression search forward/backward
	C-\\ - Toggle the configured input method

Hydra entry points:
	C-c C-y - Launcher / workgroup / media / study Hydra
	C-c C-t - Toggle editing options Hydra
	C-c C-w - Window management Hydra
	C-c C-g - Git and git-gutter Hydra
	C-c C-s - Dictionary and documentation search Hydra
	C-c C-q - Describe/help Hydra

Window Hydra (after C-c C-w):
	h/j/k/l - Move focus left/down/up/right
	q/w/e/r - Resize split left/down/up/right
	v/x - Split right/below; z/Z - Winner undo/redo
	b - Switch buffer; f - Find file; F - Follow mode
	a - Select window; s - Swap windows; S - Save buffer
	d - Delete window; D - Delete via ace-window; o/i - Keep one window
	Space - Quit the Hydra

Toggle Hydra (after C-c C-t):
	u - Toggle company-ispell; a - Abbrev mode; d - Debug on error
	f - Auto-fill; t - Truncate lines; w - Whitespace mode
	i - Toggle indent-tabs-mode; q - Quit

Git Hydra (after C-c C-g):
	dd - Diff; dc - Staged diff; dr - Diff range
	au - Stage modified files; cc - Create commit; ca - Amend commit
	tt - Stash; ta - Apply stash; l - File log; b - Show branches
	s - Show commit; k - Git link; f - Find file in commit
	ri - Interactive rebase; cr - Cherry-pick from reflog
	rr / rh - Reset gutter to default/HEAD; Q - Toggle gutter; q - Quit

Launcher Hydra (after C-c C-y):
	f/d - Recent file/directory; B/m - Set/go to bookmark
	ss/ll - Save/load workgroup; e/r - Erase/reset shell buffer
	ii - Imenu; id - Insert date; z - Jump around; q - Quit
	s1/s2 - Start 15/60 minute Pomodoro; st/sr/sp - Stop/resume/pause
	R/n/p/P/S - Shuffle/next/previous/pause/stop Emms playback

Evil mode defaults:
	h/j/k/l - Move; w/b/e - Word motions; gg/G - Buffer start/end
	i/a/o/O - Insert or open lines; v/V - Visual character/line mode
	y/d/c/p - Yank/delete/change/paste; u/C-r - Undo/redo
	/ ? n N - Search and move between matches; : - Evil Ex command
	Current config: Y yanks to end of line, Ctrl+] finds a tag, gh starts a definition
	Current config: gc/gb/gy comment, copy-comment, or yank-comment an operator motion
	Insert Ctrl-x Ctrl-n/p - Complete next/previous line; Ctrl-] - Expand snippet
	Insert Ctrl-e - End of line; Ctrl-k - Kill line; Alt-j - Expand snippet

Hydra keys are context-sensitive; use C-c C-q then b for the active bindings list.
